.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void csmp::ModelTopology::AssignMaterialProperties (\fBVSet\fP< dim > & vset, const multimap< string, \fBvector\fP< size_t > > & object_elements)"
AssignMaterialProperties() allows the user to interactively assign properties to ANSYS models via the console\&. This is tedious and we recommend to use a configuration file for this purpose\&.

.PP
The only properties that can be assigned are element properties, ie, piecewise constant material properties\&.

.PP
The method adds the property data to the argument \fBVSet\fP\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The methods takes a const reference to the model topology object\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The user is prompted for region and property names\&. 
.SS "bool csmp::ModelTopology::BoxShapedModel () const"

.PP
checks that 3D model contains the boundaries LEFT, RIGHT, BOTTOM, FRONT, BACK; TOP omitted because it may be IRREGULAR A box-shaped model has walls that lie in the XY, XZ, and YZ planes of the coordinate system\&. These wall must be identified by groups of surface elements with the correct CSP names LEFT, RIGHT, BOTTOM, TOP, FRONT and BACK\&. If these boundary identifying surfaces are present the topology is interpreted as box shaped\&. A model can also be box shaped if the top boundary is not present but a surface exists in its place that is called IRREGULAR\&. 
.br

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
If the model contains the aforementioned boundary surfaces 'true' is returned, else 'false'\&. 
.RE
.PP

