.SS "bool csmp::ModelTopology::CheckCellNumbering () const"
Tests whether the element numbers stored in \fBModelTopology\fP are in a format suitable for reorganising the \fBVSet\fP\&. The following tests are made:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
does the element numbering start with zero?
.IP "\(bu" 2
is the largest element number equivalent to the number of elements-1?
.IP "\(bu" 2
are the elements numbered consecutively?
.IP "\(bu" 2
are the elemnt ids' within each Domain consecutive\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
are there any duplicate elements?
.PP

.PP
The method assumes that that each element can only belong to a single region\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Boolean\&. If any of the tests fails the method returns false\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method complains if the element numbering does not start at 0 or the largest element number is not equal to nn-elements-1\&. 
