.SS "bool csmp::ModelTopology::IsoparametricFiniteElements () const"

.PP
type of elements A finite element mesh can either be treated as isoparametric (using a local coordinates system to define the interpolation functions and numeric integration) or as standard\&. straight-sided elements defined in physical space\&. CSMP uses different element type names to differentiate the two families of elements\&. Thus it is important to let it know your the desired approach as this will later affect the FEM formulation and available integrals\&.

.PP
The default is 'isoparametric' elements\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This method returns whether the current model is treated as isoparametric or not\&. 
.RE
.PP

