.SS "size_t csmp::ModelTopology::MinimumSpatialDimensionOfDomain (const char * region) const"
The minimum spatial dimension of a model region is taken to be one if it consists of line elements, and 2 or 3 if it is made up entirely of surface or volume elements, respectively\&. For regions that contain lines, surfaces and or volumes, the elements of highest spatial dimensionality determine the result\&. Still, this result is only a minimum estimate, because line and surface elements also exist in 3D space\&. 
.br

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIregion\fP The method takes to model region name as input argument\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The method returns the minimum spatial dimension of the target region\&. For line elements this is 1, for surfaces 2, and for volumes 3\&. 
.br
.RE
.PP
If the region cannot be found, the spatial dimension of the model will be returned in stead\&. 
.br
.SH "Messages"
.PP
When the region cannot be found, the method will report an error\&. 
